 # Changelog
 
+## Unreleased — review follow-up
+
+### Adaptive sorted-set algebra
+
+- Sorted intersection, difference, `is_subset`, `is_disjoint`, and every
+  scalar count now use an adaptive merge with `TimSort`-style galloping. Skewed
+  inputs cost `O(n · log(m / n))` comparisons instead of `O(n + m)`; the
+  64-vs-1,048,576 intersection dropped from about 1.3 ms to about 4 µs on the
+  recorded host, and is now within 2–3× of `BTreeSet` instead of 40–770× slower.
+  Balanced inputs keep the plain merge's comparison count and pay a counter
+  update per step. Union and symmetric-difference traversal are unchanged.
+- The benchmark gains skewed ordered cases against `std::collections::BTreeSet`;
+  `SET_OPERATIONS.md` records the before/after measurements.
+- New regressions: comparison budgets for skewed inputs, skewed and mixed-regime
+  property tests against standard sets, and an exhaustive lower-bound gallop
+  check.
+
+### Snapshot publication
+
+- `SnapshotStore::load_guard` and `SnapshotStore::peek` read the current version
+  through `arc-swap`'s wait-free guard instead of cloning the `Arc`; under two
+  contending readers `peek` was 17× faster than `load` on the recorded host.
+- `SnapshotStore::publish_if_current` (compare-and-swap on version identity)
+  and `SnapshotStore::update` (read-copy-update loop) make a load/derive/publish
+  sequence lossless under concurrent writers. `publish` and `load` are unchanged.
+
